From 8e714ad8eeb17b1bf2f68f3fc3f46a43789eff14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: packager <a@b.c>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:33:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The launch cuts and the new rulings: many sevas, eight
 digits, silk ivory, one uniform bell button, and rows the dashboard can
 delete (round 40)

At full launch the testing-phase furniture leaves, exactly as promised
when it was added: the omkar-diag receipt stamp goes out of the service
worker, the bell panel's diagnostic line and its three content keys go
out of the panel and both languages, and the round-38 guard test keeps
only the handler guards that stay forever. Enable and Disable now wear
the very same button - same size, same shape - at the owner's ruling.

The owner's new rulings, all bilingual where text moves:
  - seva cards are a multi-select (aria-pressed, checkbox mark); the
    submission lists every chosen seva, joined with + in the row;
  - the seva contact field is an Oman number: digits only, max length
    eight, and submit refuses anything that is not exactly eight
    (contactDigits flash in EN and KN);
  - the first seva is Prasada/Naivedya, and Incense/Dhoop becomes
    Abhisheka - pouring of sacred liquids over Hanuman's idol,
    mirrored in Kannada;
  - the caption under the name ends '...through devotion, music and
    knowledge' in English, mirrored in Kannada with jnanada moola;
  - the light ground is the owner's silk ivory, #F6EBDD;
  - the dashboard gains a per-row Delete on seva signups and on
    messages, behind a confirm; the admin_delete RLS policies and
    grants for both tables already exist since migration 0001, so no
    SQL change is needed.

tests/round40-launch-cuts.test.js pins every cut and ruling; all of its
guards fail on the bare round-39 tree.
